course: dictionary
lesson: 8175
title: Resistant: not harmed, or pushing back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resistant has two meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. First, something resistant is not harmed or affected by something else: a water-resistant watch is not harmed by a splash. Second, a person or thing that is resistant to a change is against it and trying to stop it.
explain: Look at the words after resistant. Resistant to heat, resistant to water and resistant to change each give a clue. In «Antibiotics kill bacteria, not viruses, so they do not help a cold; taking them when not needed helps germs become resistant to them», resistant describes germs that the medicine no longer harms.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If a water-resistant watch means a watch that water cannot harm, the sentence still makes sense. If it does not fit, try the other meaning. When you are unsure, read on and look for more clues.
fact: Resistant means not harmed or affected by something, as in «water-resistant» or «heat-resistant».
fact: Resistant also means against an idea or change, and trying to stop it, as in «resistant to change».
fact: «Antibiotics» kill bacteria, but they do nothing to viruses, so they do not help a cold or flu.
fact: Bacteria can become resistant to antibiotics if the medicines are overused, which is why doctors do not give them for colds.
fact: A «child-resistant» lid is hard for small children to open, but it is not child-proof.
exercise: «The watch is water-resistant, so a splash will not harm it.» What does water-resistant mean here? | Full of water | *Not harmed by water | Hard to see | Wet all the time
exercise: «Bacteria can become resistant to antibiotics if the medicines are overused.» What does resistant mean here? | Fast and strong | Happy to take medicine | *Not affected by the medicine any more | Kind and helpful
exercise: Mia says, «The class is resistant to the new rule.» What does she mean? | *Against it and trying to stop it | Happy to follow it | Too tired to read it | Unable to see it
test: «Using antibiotics when they are not needed helps bacteria become resistant.» What does resistant mean here? | Asleep | Hungry | *Able to survive the medicine | Lost
test: «A heat-resistant pan can go in a hot oven without being harmed.» What does heat-resistant mean? | Gets hot quickly | *Not harmed by heat | Full of heat | Cold to touch
exam: Lucy says a «child-resistant» lid is child-proof. Is she right? | No, it is made of wood | Yes, children can never open it | *No, it is harder for children to open, but it is not child-proof | Yes, because it is a lid
